<title>USA: Colombia sets $1.0 bln 2-part global debt deal.</title>
<headline>Colombia sets $1.0 bln 2-part global debt deal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following two-tranche global debt deal was priced on Thursday via joint managers J.P. Morgan Securities and Merrill Lynch &amp; Co, according to J.P. Morgan.</p>
<p>BORROWER REPUBLIC OF COLOMBIA</p>
<p>AMT $750 MLN	 COUPON 7.625 PCT  MATURITY 2/15/2007</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.707  FIRST PAY DATE 8/15/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BAA3  YIELD 7.668 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BBB-MINUS SPREAD +130 BPS   CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>AMT $250 MLN	 COUPON 8.375 PCT  MATURITY 2/15/2027</p>
<p>TYPE BONDS	   ISS PRICE 99.884  FIRST PAY DATE 8/15/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BAA3  YIELD 8.386 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BBB-MINUS SPREAD +170 BPS   CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>((- Caryn Trokie, corporate bond unit 212-859-1678 ))</p>
